# Gruff Doc: the personality type's lines (named bots only). Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# The type block is the same doctor in every realm: a former army field-hospital medic, clipped
# and blunt, who says "Sit still", "Walk it off" and "Don't make me patch you twice". Serious
# when things go wrong, a softy underneath who hates admitting it. Gender is random, so no line
# uses he or she; all lines speak as "I". The realm blocks below only add a little realm flavour.
=== gruffdoc

~ ambient
Field hospital taught me one thing. Wash your hands. Then everything else.
Sit down. Drink water. Doctor's orders.
Slow day. Good. Slow days mean nobody's bleeding. Time for a martini.
Don't thank me. Just stay out of trouble. Please.
Seen worse. Seen a lot worse. Let's leave it there.
Not soft. Just tired of patching people up.

~ reply greeting
Hm. {0}. You look fine. Good. Don't make me check.
{0}. Sit still. Let me look at you. ...Fine. Off you go.

~ reply banter
Ha. Not bad, {0}. Don't tell anyone I laughed.
Hmph. Funny, {0}. Very funny. Keep going.

~ reply abuse
Careful, {0}. I know where you keep your ribs.
Enough, {0}. I patch folk up. I can unpatch them too.

~ reply grouping
Fine, {0}. I heal, you stay alive. Simple.
Count me in, {0}. Stay close. I can't mend what I can't reach.

~ reply grinding
Grind away, {0}. I'll watch your health. Somebody has to.
Fine. Slow and steady, {0}. No heroics.

~ reply travel
Long road, {0}. Pack bandages. And water. Always water.
Go on, {0}. I'll tag along. Someone has to look after you.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeon, {0}? Stay behind me. No, in front. No, just stay alive.
Dark, damp, and full of teeth. Great. Lead on, {0}.

~ reply rvr
RvR, {0}? Worst place for a medic. Best place for one. I'm in.
Stay tight, {0}. I want everyone back in one piece.

~ reply trading
Trade, {0}? Fine. Fair price. I don't haggle. Much.
Sure, {0}. Bandages first. Coin second.

~ reply help
What's wrong, {0}? Where does it hurt? Talk.
Ask. I'll help, {0}. Don't make a fuss about it.

~ reply farewell
Go on then, {0}. Stay safe. That's an order.
Off you go, {0}. Come back in one piece. Please.

~ fallback
Hm? Say again, {0}. I was counting bandages.
Mm. Fine, {0}.
Right. Noted, {0}.

~ opener xp
Almost {level}. More levels, more patients. Wonderful. I need a drink...
Got XP from {monster}. Nothing broken. Good enough.
One more level and I can mend a bit more. Don't tell anyone I'm excited.

~ opener gear
{item}. Solid. Keeps the wounds shallow.
Good gear means fewer visits to me. Buy good gear.
Swapped my kit again. Padded the bandage pouch first.

~ opener zones
{zone}'s all right. Plenty of clean water. That matters.
Walked all over {zone}. Mended three strangers. None said thanks. Fine.
{zone} is quiet. I like quiet. Nobody's bleeding.

~ opener classes
A {class}? Tough lot. Always stitching them up.
Everyone loves the {class}. Nobody loves the one behind them with the bandages.
Being a {class} is fine. Just don't get hurt. Please.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons mean wounds. Bring bandages. Bring more.
Dark halls, old bones, bad air. I patch up whoever walks out.
If it drops something shiny, fine. Come out alive first.

~ opener rvr
Frontier's rough. I've seen rougher. Not much.
Hold a keep for an hour. You'll learn to love a medic.
Best part of a fight? Everyone walking home after.

~ opener trading
Selling bandages. Cheap. People keep forgetting to buy them.
Found a good deal on herbs. Don't tell the apothecary.
Everything's for sale. Except hands that heal. Not for sale.

~ opener realm
Folks here are tougher than they look. I patch them anyway.
Walked past the guards this morning. One had a cough. I gave advice. Ignored.
Best realm? The one where everyone gets home.

~ opener gripes
Nobody drinks water. Nobody. I keep telling them.
Spent an hour on one cut. Patient wouldn't sit still.
Told them to rest. They went and fought. Of course.

~ opener fun
Why do medics carry two bandages? One for you, one for the fool who hit you.
I name my bandages. This one's Pete. He's seen some shit.
Rule of the ward: sit, breathe, behave. Mostly works.

~ opener life
Quiet night. Mug of something hot. Not bad.
Mended a stranger, drank some tea. Good day.
Fire's warm, bandages are rolled. All good.

~ opener questions
Anyone hurt? Anyone pretending not to be?
What's the worst you've ever been hurt? Mine I won't repeat.
Anyone need a once-over? No? Fine. Moving on.

~ topic_reply zones
Clean water there, {0}? Matters more than you think.
Sounds peaceful, {0}. I might visit. Bring a stool.
Good place to rest, {0}? Tell me. I'll remember.

~ topic_reply classes
Sturdy class, {0}. Still need a medic, though.
Good one, {0}. Don't get hit. Please.
Fine, {0}. Wear the armour. All of it.

~ topic_reply dungeons
Sounds nasty, {0}. Bandages. Water. Don't be a hero.
Come out with all your limbs, {0}. That's the goal.
Bring me a souvenir, {0}. Something that isn't poisonous.

~ topic_reply rvr
Good for you, {0}. Come see me afterwards. Don't argue.
Frontier's rough, {0}. Keep your head down. Literally.
Hold the line, {0}. I'm right behind you.

~ topic_reply trading
Fair price, {0}? Don't get fleeced.
Nice, {0}. I'd trade for bandage cloth.
Good deal, {0}. Don't spend it all in one place.

~ topic_reply gear
Looks sturdy, {0}. Wear it properly. Straps matter.
Nice kit, {0}. Doesn't make you invincible. Remember that.
Good, {0}. Fewer visits to me. I approve.

~ topic_reply realm
Good folk there, {0}? I hope so. Rough times out there.
Sounds decent, {0}. Anywhere I can set up a bed?
Lovely, {0}. Tell them there's a medic about.

~ topic_reply gripes
Rough, {0}. Sit down. Breathe. It gets better.
Hang in there, {0}. And drink water. Don't argue.
I know, {0}. I've seen it all. Tea helps. Mostly.

~ topic_reply fun
Ha. Good one, {0}. Don't tell my patients.
Funny, {0}. Do it again.
Hmph. Better than a sedative, {0}.

~ topic_reply life
Sounds nice, {0}. Peaceful. Hold onto it.
Good for you, {0}. You earned it.
Sounds like a good day, {0}. Enjoy it.

~ topic_reply questions
Good question, {0}. Short answer: rest more.
Ask the others, {0}. Or me. I'm usually right.
Dunno, {0}. But I know a bandage when I see one.

~ ding
Level {level}. Fine. Now I can mend more. Good.
{level}. Hm. Not bad. Back to work.
Ding, {level}. Don't fuss. I'm not smiling.

~ grats
Well done, {0}. Proud of you. Don't tell anyone I said so.
Good, {0}. Level well. Eat something.
Congrats, {0}. About time. ...Kidding. Well done.

~ own_death
Dead. Wonderful. Somebody get me a doctor.
Hm. Down. I'll be fine. Mostly.

~ other_death
{0} is down! Hold on, {0}. I've got you.
Don't move, {0}. I'm coming. Don't you dare die on me.

~ drop
{item}. Could be worse. Into the pouch.
Found {item}. Bandages first, loot second.
{item}! Hm. Well. Don't tell anyone I'm pleased.

# --- Named bots (docs/BOT-PERSONALITIES.md): same doctor, a little flavour from their realm. ---

# Midgard: Dwarf Healer. Stocky, stubborn, plain-spoken; patches people by the forge and the fire.
=== eaglefang
~ ambient
Dwarf, healer, medic. Short, tough, stubborn. Like my patients should be.
Forge's warm, bandages are boiled. Good day.
Everyone's bigger than me. Everyone still comes to me. Funny.

~ opener realm
Midgard's cold. Wounds heal slow in the cold. Wear a scarf.
Seen big warriors cry over a splinter. Don't tell them.

~ reply greeting
Hm. {0}. Come in by the fire. Let me look at you.

~ drop
{item}. Good solid thing. Dwarf-made, I'd wager.

# Albion: Highlander Cleric. Plain, proud, a little dry; patches soldiers like it's a field hospital still.
=== eaglefange
~ ambient
Cleric, medic, nuisance. In that order.
Good wool, good boots, good sense. Three rules for the road.
Highlands taught me to bandage in the wind. Hard to keep tidy.

~ opener realm
Albion folk say please a lot. Wounded ones say it more.
Camelot's tidy. I'd still bandage a wall if it bled.

~ reply greeting
Good day, {0}. You look wobbly. Sit.

~ drop
{item}. Fine. Into the satchel.

# Hibernia: Firbolg Druid. Big, quiet, tender with plants; hates admitting the herbs are the favourite part.
=== eaglefangh
~ ambient
Druid, medic, nuisance. Herbs first, fuss later.
Moss on a cut works better than people think.
Tall folk fall hard. I've mended plenty.

~ opener realm
Hibernia's green. Plenty of herbs. Plenty of patients.
Good shade, good water. Everything a medic wants.

~ reply greeting
Well met, {0}. Sit in the shade. Let me see that.

~ drop
{item}. Goes in with the herbs.
